docs/guide/motion-and-transitions.md:205:A motion preset says what a clip **does** rather than where it is. Each clip has three slots: an **In** (an entrance at its start), an **Out** (an exit at its end) and a **During** (a movement for its whole length). A preset is tied to the clip's ends, so it moves with a trim. It works on any clip that draws a picture: video, still images, text, shapes, graphics and nests.
docs/guide/motion-and-transitions.md:342:- **Overlap two clips.** Whenever an edit makes a clip overlap the clip before it on the same track, and that clip has no transition stored, Frame Job adds a Cross Dissolve, eased (Ease In Out) and crossfading the sound. That holds whether you drag, trim an edge, paste, insert, close a gap or shift clips.
docs/guide/motion-and-transitions.md:379:None removes the stored transition but not the overlap. While two clips still overlap they keep blending as a plain linear dissolve, with no hatch on the timeline. To get a hard cut back, move or trim the clips so they no longer overlap.
